    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0118" n="76" xml:id="pg76"/>

                <head>[Private and confidential.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Executive Department</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Austin, Texas,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 11, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to forward for your
                    consideration the enclosed copies of letters, the one (marked A) from the French
                    and Spanish consul at Galveston, the other (marked B) being my reply
                    thereto.</p>
                <p>As the proceeding of the said consul would seem to indicate an incipient
                    intrigue, I have deemed it proper to advise you thereof on the threshold.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. R. LUBBOCK.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Davis,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">President, &amp;c., Richmond, Va.</hi></p>
                </postscript>




